 "headline": {
  "free_only_direction_if_adopted": "looser, not stricter: free-only lands at ~0.997-0.998 of the drop on the same records where free+inactive scores 0.4965-0.5173. Switching to it after seeing BLOCKED trials would move the goalpost in the passing direction.",
  "hypothesis_result": "NOT supported by these records. The inactive component contributes 0.0033 at most of the scored gain, because inactive falls during the settle window instead of rising: the host arrives at the anchor with a nearly empty free pool (~0.13-0.25 GiB) and a large pre-existing inactive backlog (~13 GiB), and reclaiming that backlog is what fills free. free+inactive therefore nets the backlog off and is the CONSERVATIVE of the two readings.",
  "hypothesis_tested": "free+inactive over-credits the kernel by counting pages the target released that the kernel has not reclaimed yet",
  "inactive_share_of_gain_max": 0.0033,
  "inactive_share_of_gain_min": 0.0,
  "kernel_resident_drop_range_bytes": [
   17284706040,
   17300188920
  ],
  "ratio_free_only_range": [
   0.996158,
   0.998814
  ],
  "ratio_free_plus_inactive_range": [
   0.496538,
   0.517308
  ],
  "what_the_numbers_actually_track": "gain = peak(free+inactive) - anchor(free+inactive). Across the five trials the resident drop is stable (~16.1 GiB) while the gain spans ~8.00-8.34 GiB and the threshold is ~8.05 GiB, i.e. the 0.50 line sits INSIDE the trial-to-trial spread and the starting pool state of the host is in the measurement. That is why the remedy registered for future claims is repetition on the same executable, not a different numerator."
 },
 "not_claimed": [
  "no verdict is re-decided here; each trial keeps what its own verifier run wrote",
  "the free-only ratio is reported without a threshold on purpose",
  "adopting free-only after seeing these numbers would be moving the goalposts; it can only be used if it is registered before a future run",
  "this is a decomposition of already-recorded bytes, not a new experiment",
  "no claim here says the product did or did not return pages; A1-A9 carry that"
